Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T12:57:05-07:00","id":1495263,"title":"","content":"I mostly said gehenna got cancelled when one of the third got vacuum aid bombed by 2nd inq easy fix","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T20:07:42-07:00","id":1495299,"title":"","content":"In an alternate timeline, all of the above incidents are canon and the 5th Edition line of games are explicitly about life in the Sixth Age of the Wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T12:48:51-07:00","id":1495456,"title":"","content":"1: For most of human history there have always been at least a few groups thinking that the past was near-infinitely long and the end is nigh: If the apocalypse doesn't happen tomorrow it doesn't mean it's not going to happen it just means we need to adjust our calculations a little. Maybe our egos just make us want to believe existence should culminate with us and the universe can't do without us. <br /> <br /> 2: VTM metaplot was garbage old WW churned out because it was an easy method to keep book sales up. Quantity at the expense of quality. The best stuff WW wrote has always been detached from the metaplot. <br /> <br /> For these reasons I'm always happy to push Gehenna back as far as I please. But the idea of a cycle gehenna is just pants because you've got neither the fear mongering working atmosphere and wonders into the tapestry of politics nor the balls-to-the-wall drive of an actual vampiric apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I dread that there's a tiger at my door and then when I open it find that it's a housecat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T02:08:27-07:00","id":1495471,"title":"","content":"The options I see for an apocalypse are:<ul><li>a) The Apocalypse is sort-of happening but rather than a world-ending event it's a calamitous event happening on a huge scale and affecting a lot of people. Stuff like the Late Bronze Age Collapse, the Plague or the two World-Wars. It isn't the end of the world but to the people experiencing those disastrous situations, it certainly can feel like that.</li> <li>b) There's a prophecy predicting the end of the world and... it's wrong. There's no apocalypse coming.</li> <li>c) The world is gonna end but actions can be taken to avoid that.</li> <li>d) The world is gonna end. No ifs or buts.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> With the &quot;Gehenna is cyclical&quot;-idea I would've expected something like a) to happen but the actual V5-book felt more like b). And depending on where things could've gone with the Beckoning and the Gehenna-war in the Middle East, I guess, it could've turned into a c) or d).<br /> <br /> I wonder where &quot;Gaia is dead/dying&quot; will fall in how it's depicted.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, I've never once played an endtimes-scenario with any of the WOD-games. It was fun to read about at times but I could never imagine playing through these scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}